            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "chassishandler.cpp",
                    "line": 1034,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "I would prefer that the name remains getButtonEnabled since the property name is \"Enabled\". Instead, change the variables and stuff inside of the function to return the appropriate value.\n\nwhile you are refactoring here, please turn the dbus calls into yielding calls instead of blocking calls.\n```suggestion\nstatic std::optional<bool> getButtonEnabled(ipmi::Context::ptr& ctx, const std::string& buttonPath,\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassishandler.cpp",
                    "line": 1034,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "If `x86-power-control` is used, the actual property name that should be used is `ButtonMasked`. So in this case it is really \"ButtonDisabled\"\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/x86-power-control/blob/2947720bc30cdc081ebe2ecaba093268cf115b90/src/power_control.cpp#L3312\n\nIf we want to be able to handle both implementations, wouldn't it be better to stick with the IPMI naming? Since IPMI spec cares about button disable funtionality particularly.\n\nAs for the yielding calls, I've already did that, please see next patch in the chain \"78253: Use ctx in getButtonDisabled function\" | https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-host-ipmid/+/78253"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassishandler.cpp",
                    "line": 1034,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "Okay. Seems like good enough logic. This is an IPMI daemon after all. x86-power-control should get onboard and use a standard naming scheme."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassishandler.cpp",
                    "line": 1055,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "Don't change the name; it should match the property name."
                }
            ],
